    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, can you give me a quick breakdown of the standard stages for a CI/CD pipeline? I'm drafting a doc for my team at a fintech firm. Specifically, I need to cover code commit, automated testing, staging, and production deployment, and what kind of gates we should have at each stage to prevent bad code from moving forward. Thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A typical CI/CD pipeline for a fintech firm should begin with an immediate build and unit test upon code commit to ensure basic functionality and type safety. Next, automated integration and security scanning (critical for financial data) validate that components work together and no vulnerabilities exist before promotion to the staging environment. Once in staging, regression and load testing gates confirm system stability under realistic financial transaction scenarios. Finally, pre-production gate checks—such as compliance audits and human approval—must be mandatory before any code reaches the live environment to prevent outages or data breaches. These sequential gates ensure only robust, secure, and tested code affects your customers.",
      "source": "target",
