      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Unseen failures often occur when teams optimize build times by skipping deep dependency checks or approximating security scans, leading to critical flaws bypassing automated gates. Additionally, edge cases in complex financial logic may pass unit tests but fail in real-world scenarios due to environments that don't fully emulate market volatility or loyalty program interactions. To manage this risk, you should frame it as \"yielding false positives in automated checks vs. missing rare edge cases\" which is why every complex transaction path must have a manual override check by a domain expert. This distinction helps stakeholders understand that automation catches 90% of risks, while human judgment fills the critical gaps remaining in the pipeline.",
